# The code licence is pending a decision by Butler University, so this file has no
# license field for the software. The data files are dedicated to the public domain
# under CC0 1.0 (see the data reference below).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these files, please cite the paper (preferred-citation) and the table of Carmichael numbers (references)."
type: software
title: "The Prime Wavelet Tree: code and files for compressing the Carmichael numbers below 10^24"
abstract: >-
  Code that writes, decodes and certifies eight lossless representations of
  the table of all Carmichael numbers below 10^24 (the A/B/C matrix of the
  paper) and a prime wavelet tree over heuristically chosen divisors, with the
  commands, expected hashes and run logs behind every reported number.
